  "texts": {
    "preamble": "N. Binu vs State Of Kerala on 9 October, 2024 Author: P.V.Kunhikrishnan Bench: P.V.Kunhikrishnan Crl.M.C. No.2515 of 2018 1 2024:Ker:75100 In The High Court Of Kerala At Ernakulam Present The Honourable Mr. Justice P.V.Kunhikrishnan Wednesday, The 9Th Day Of October 2024 / 17Th Aswina, 1946 Crl.Mc No. 2515 Of 2018 Against The Order/Judgment Dated In Cc No.777 Of 2015 Of Special Court Of Judicial Magistrate Of First Class For Trial Of Cases U/S.138 Ni Act(Jmfc Xi), Thiruvananthapuram Petitioner/Accused: N. Binu S/O Nadesan, Food Business Operator & License, Nadesh Bakers,T.C 5/570,571, Peroorkada P.O,Thiruvananthapuram, Residing At Nadesh Bunglow, Peroorkada P.O Thiruvananthapuram. By Advs. Sri.Shajin S.Hameed Smt.A.R.Susmitha Respondent/State: N. Binu vs State Of Kerala on 9 October, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/30023137/ 1 State Of Kerala Represented By The Food Safety Officer, Mobile Vigilance Squad,Office Of The Assistant Commissioner(Intelligence),Thycaud, Crl.M.C. No.2515 of 2018 2 2024:Ker:75100 Near Food Safety Commissioner, Thiruvananthapuram,Represented Through The Public Prosecutor, Thiruvananthapuram. By Adv.: Sri.Renjith.T.R, Sr.Pp This Criminal Misc. Case Having Been Finally Heard On 09.10.2024, The Court On The Same Day Passed The Following: Crl.M.C. No.2515 of 2018 3 2024:Ker:75100 P.V.Kunhikrishnan, J. -------------------------------- Crl.M.C. No.2515 of 2018 ---------------------------------------------- Dated this the 09th day of October, 2024 Order",
    "facts": "This Criminal Miscellaneous Case is filed to quash Annexure-A complaint. 2. The above complaint is filed by the Food Safety Officer against the petitioner under Section 3(i) (zz), (vii) of FSSA Act 2006, S.26(2)(i), S.59(i) of Food Safety and Standard Act, 2006, FSS Rule 2011 and r/w Regulations 2.12 and Regulation 3.1.2(7) of Food Safety and Standards (Food Products Standards and Food Additives) Regulations 2011.",
    "arguments": "After arguing for sometime, the learned counsel for the petitioner submitted that, the 2024:KER:75100 petitioner may be allowed to raise all these contentions before the trial court, at the appropriate stage. The counsel also submitted that the petitioner may be exempted from personal appearance.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "After arguing for sometime, the learned counsel for the petitioner submitted that, the 2024:KER:75100 petitioner may be allowed to raise all these contentions before the trial court, at the appropriate stage. The counsel also submitted that the petitioner may be exempted from personal appearance.",
